            <property name="text">
             <string>About the classification</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="about_classification_label">
            <property name="text">
             <string>&lt;b&gt;The transition frequency&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• It tells how fast a slow wave goes from its negative peak to its positive peak.&lt;br/&gt;• It is 1/(2τ), where τ is the time from the negative peak to the positive peak [1].&lt;br/&gt;• "Detect Slow Waves" writes it for each slow wave, in the column trans_freq_Hz of the slow wave characteristics files.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;The categories&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• Snooz puts together the slow waves of all the files and channels. Then it fits a Gaussian mixture to the distribution of their transition frequencies.&lt;br/&gt;• Each Gaussian component is a category of slow waves. The number of components is found automatically or set by you, in the step "Classification Criteria".&lt;br/&gt;• Each slow wave goes to the closest category, with a k-means clustering started from the means of the components.&lt;br/&gt;• The categories are numbered by transition frequency. Category 1 holds the slow waves with the slowest transitions.&lt;br/&gt;• The same categories are used for all the recordings of the cohort.</string>
            </property>
            <property name="textFormat">
             <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
            </property>
            <property name="wordWrap">
             <bool>true</bool>
            </property>
            <property name="variant" stdset="0">
             <string notr="true">help</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
